# Easily made mistakes that happened to me explained, to save you some trouble

## White 504 Error Page when trying to access the App in the Browser

start app in incognito browser or hard reload to empty the cache

## Delete your volumes before cloning the repository

If you delete the repository after you already successfully set a password for Postgres
and then proceed to clone the repo again, the Postgres instance will
start for the old project but try to connect with your newly cloned project as it has the
same name.

The Solution is to delete the old Postgres volume with `docker compose down -v` from your
project root directory. Afterwards you can start over with Setting up the database Password.

## Bash vs zsh

The README of mtg-commander-stats uses bash. If you are on zsh like me, you need to check
some commands for compatibility. This Handbook uses zsh because it was written by me, the
human PO, while the docs in the main project are written by AI agents.

README (Bash): `read -r -s -p 'Local PostgreSQL password: ' POSTGRES_PASSWORD`
Handbook (zsh): 'read -rs "POSTGRES_PASSWORD?Local PostgreSQL password:"